INT. PARKING GARAGE LEVEL P4 - NIGHT

Concrete. Sodium light. A single car, hood up.

NORA VESS, 30s, journalist. Leather jacket. She stands behind a pillar.

Thirty feet away, in the car's glow, a woman waits. DR. ELISE MARCHETTI, 50s. Raincoat. A briefcase.

Nora steps out.

NORA
You're early.

ELISE
So are you.

NORA
You said midnight.

ELISE
I said when it was safe.

Nora walks closer. Her heels echo. Elise watches.

NORA
Is it safe?

ELISE
No.

NORA
Then why are we here?

ELISE
Because it won't get safer.

Elise sets the briefcase on the hood. Her hands tremble. She lifts the latches.

ELISE (CONT'D)
Before I open this. One condition.

NORA
Name it.

ELISE
My name stays out of it.

NORA
Your name is the story.

ELISE
Then there's no story.

Nora folds her arms. Elise doesn't blink.

NORA
You called me.

ELISE
I know.

NORA
You said they'd kill you.

ELISE
I said they might.

NORA
Does that change the condition?

ELISE
It makes it firm.

A car engine growls somewhere above. Both women look up. The sound passes.

NORA
Where do they park?

ELISE
Level two. Executive spaces.

NORA
Then we have time.

ELISE
We have fifteen minutes.

Nora pulls a recorder from her jacket and sets it on the hood beside the case. She presses record. A red light glows.

NORA
Say it for the tape.

ELISE
I can't.

NORA
Then show me.

Elise opens the lid. Papers, hundreds of them, and a small drive. She lifts a page and holds it under the light.

ELISE
Lot four-four-one-seven. The shipment dates are wrong.

NORA
Wrong how?

ELISE
Backdated. All of them.

NORA
By how long?

ELISE
Six months.

NORA
That's fraud.

ELISE
It's worse.

She hands the page across. Nora reads. Her lips move. She looks up.

NORA
Those are drug trials.

ELISE
Yes.

NORA
Patients died.

ELISE
Eleven.

NORA
And they knew.

ELISE
They knew in March.

Nora lets the page fall to the hood. Her face is pale.

NORA
You signed the reports.

ELISE
I did.

NORA
Then you're in it.

ELISE
I know.

NORA
So why come to me?

ELISE
Because I'd rather go down with the truth than up with the lie.

Nora studies her. The light buzzes overhead. In the distance, a second engine starts.

NORA
Keep talking.

ELISE
Not here.

NORA
Where?

ELISE
Take the case. Go.

NORA
And you?

ELISE
(a thin smile)
I'll be right behind you.

Nora snaps the case shut, lifts it, and backs toward the ramp. Elise watches her go. The engine closes in.
